{
  "_doc": "v79.12.7: the penal reasoning's tables (src/rag/penal_lines.py). jurisprudential_elements: an element the law's text does not state but the lawyer's note di inquadramento (article_notes) or a kept ruling passage (rulings.build's kept) does -- found by its patterns in that text, it enters the record as inferred, «da provare», its source named; contesting it is sostenibile. absorption: titles never offered as autonomous beside their absorber (mode «absorbed»: out of the records; «alternative_only»: kept only as the riqualificazione alternative) or where the facts narrate a soccorso (mode «post_fact»: out, the soccorso a favourable element after the fact). requalify_elements: a riqualificazione between these articles is offered only naming the element that differs and the facts bearing on it (fact_patterns, read in the case's sentences). causation_realism: a causation defence (art. 41 c.p.) on an ordinary consequence is capped at realismo basso unless a trigger fact is narrated; a reply denying the causal link is replaced by the subjective-element reply. Patterns are Python regexes, case-insensitive. circumstance_triggers (v79.12.7, item 2): the attenuanti read from the facts, replacing the fixed attenuanti block -- an attenuante is printed when a case sentence holds one of its «patterns» (62 n. 2: a diverbio, a provocazione, an offesa; its «point» the open question tied to it), one of its «steps» (62 n. 6: the concrete step named) or one of its «support_patterns» (62-bis: with record support only; with «post_fact» true the soccorso narrated -- the «post_fact» absorption rule's patterns -- counts as the favourable element after the fact); a hit the «negation_pattern» precedes (within 40 characters) does not count. «absent»: what is printed when nothing in the facts triggers it -- «omit» (not printed) or «to_verify» (its «to_verify» line); never «esclusa», which only a record excluding it by a contradicting sentence prints. bilanciamento: the art. 69 c.p. line whenever an aggravante is in the record. exclusion_patterns / not_exclusion_patterns: a written sentence saying a circumstance is excluded (rewritten to «da verificare» unless the record excludes it). Review: «denial_patterns» -- a note or passage saying the jurisprudential element is NOT required is no source of it; «not_by_offender_patterns» -- a soccorso in a clause naming someone else who gave it (or a passive) is not the offender's, and the place «pronto soccorso» is none; the riqualificazione's «negation_pattern» and the causation rule's «trigger_negation_pattern» -- a fact the sentence denies counts for nothing; 62 n. 6's «step_exclude_patterns» -- the victim's claim is no step; «rite_prose» -- a written sentence on a computed rito stating a figure the computation does not print, or the resulting pena with no figure, is dropped.",
